---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "acceptance", label: "Acceptance" },
  { id: "use", label: "Use of the tools" },
  { id: "no-warranty", label: "No warranty" },
  { id: "liability", label: "Limitation of liability" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes" },
  { id: "note", label: "About this document" },
];
---

<DocLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="Plain-language terms of use for Free JSON Toolkit: the tools are provided as-is, your data stays on your machine, and you use the service at your own risk."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede="The terms of using a site that never stores your data are refreshingly short. Here they are, in plain language."
  toc={toc}
  updated="2026-07-30"
  tag="Plain-language"
  notice="Plain-language summary — not a substitute for formal legal advice. If you rely on this service for regulated or commercial use, have qualified counsel review it."
>
  <section class="doc-section" id="acceptance">
    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By using Free JSON Toolkit you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, the right move is
      simply not to use the tools — and because nothing is stored about you, walking away leaves no
      trace on our side.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="use">
    <h2>Use of the tools</h2>
    <p>
      The tools are provided free of charge for lawful, personal, and professional use. You are
      responsible for the content you paste or upload and for verifying that any output is correct
      before you rely on it. Do not use the tools to process data in a way that violates any law or
      third-party right that applies to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="no-warranty">
    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The toolkit is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>, without warranty of any kind, express or
      implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
      purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the tools will be uninterrupted,
      error-free, or that results will be accurate for every input.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="liability">
    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the project and its maintainers are not liable for any
      indirect, incidental, or consequential loss arising from use of the tools, including loss of
      data or reliance on output. Because your data is processed on your own machine and never
      stored by us, we have no copy of it to lose or disclose — but you should still treat the
      service as you would any local utility and keep your own backups.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="changes">
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated from time to time. The "Updated" date at the top of this page
      reflects the latest revision. Continued use after a change constitutes acceptance of the
      revised terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" id="note">
    <h2>About this document</h2>
    <p>
      This page is written to be readable, not to be a wall of legalese. It captures the practical
      reality of a free, account-less, local-first tool. For binding legal terms tailored to a
      specific jurisdiction or commercial context, consult a qualified lawyer.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocLayout>
